# Docker build context denylist (#55). The image's contents are already fully determined by the
# Dockerfile's three explicit COPYs (pb_hooks/, pb_migrations/, pb_public/) — this file exists for
# two other reasons: (a) build-context size (a local pb_data/ can be many GB, and the local
# ./pocketbase binary alone is ~30 MB and would get re-uploaded to the daemon on every build), and
# (b) never letting local secrets or repo metadata into a build context, even though none of it is
# actually COPYed in.

pb_data/
pb_diag_data/
pb_test_data/
pocketbase
pocketbase.exe
tests/
node_modules/
.git/
.github/
.claude/

# `env` is a gitignored root-level file for local secrets (see .gitignore); .env/.env.* cover the
# more conventional naming. CLAUDE.local.md is this repo's own gitignored spot for personal local
# overrides (see CLAUDE.md) — same risk, same treatment.
.env
.env.*
env
CLAUDE.local.md

package.json
package-lock.json
README.md
CLAUDE.md
.gitignore
